{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of the hospital doctors. You're here because of severe abdominal pain and diarrhea. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. For the last few days, I’ve been going to the bathroom every 20 to 30 minutes—up to 40 times a day. It’s watery, not bloody, but the pain in my lower left belly is terrible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That sounds very uncomfortable. You mentioned this feels similar to past Crohn’s flares?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:26:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s just like before—same kind of cramping, same urgency. But this time it came on fast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:27:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had a subtotal colectomy, so you don’t have a colon anymore, but the inflammation can still happen in your small intestine and rectum."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. And I’ve been on prednisone at home—30 mg daily, up from 15 mg. But it’s not helping enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:29:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed your labs. Your white count is a bit high, and your bicarbonate is low—14—which suggests metabolic acidosis, possibly from dehydration due to the diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:30:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been drinking, but I can’t keep up. I also feel lightheaded sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:31:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’re going to keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now to let your bowel rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:32:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Nothing to eat or drink? Even water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:32:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you IV fluids to keep you hydrated. You can’t eat or drink yet, but we’ll reassess tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:33:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. But please, I need something for the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:34:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given you IV hydromorphone in the ER, and we’ll continue pain control. We also started IV steroids—methylprednisolone—to reduce the inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:35:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Steroids again? I’m already on prednisone. Is this safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:36:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because this is a flare, we need higher-dose IV steroids to get it under control quickly. We’ll transition back to oral prednisone as you improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:37:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on steroids for years. I lost my left testicle—got hard after long-term use. I worry about side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:38:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand your concern. We’re using this short-term to treat the flare. Your gastroenterologist will help you taper slowly to minimize side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2180-08-18 13:39:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your pain is a bit better today, I hear. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still painful, but not as intense. I haven’t had the urge to go as often—maybe 10 times since last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:17:35",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign. Your labs this morning show your bicarbonate is improving—up to 20. Your kidney function is also better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:18:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the IV fluids are helping?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:19:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and the steroids are starting to work. The GI team recommends starting clear liquids today—water, broth, apple juice—see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:20:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have coffee? I usually drink a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. Caffeine can irritate your gut. We’ll keep it caffeine-free and low-residue for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood. What about my omeprazole for acid reflux?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve been giving you IV pantoprazole, which is similar. Once you’re on full oral intake, we’ll switch back to your usual omeprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2180-08-19 09:24:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had GERD for years. Don’t want that flaring too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with clear liquids. We’re advancing you to a low-residue, lactose-free diet—soft foods like mashed potatoes, applesauce, and toast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds better than nothing. How long until I can eat normally?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It depends on how you respond. If your bowel movements stay controlled, we’ll keep progressing. We also got your stool tests back—no infection found."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not food poisoning or something I caught?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:34:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. No C. diff, no Salmonella, Shigella, or parasites. This looks like a Crohn’s flare, not an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:35:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about that. So the steroids are doing the job?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:36:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re switching from IV to oral prednisone today—60 mg daily. You’ll need to taper it slowly with your gastroenterologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:37:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "60 mg? That’s higher than I was on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:38:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but only for a short burst to control the flare. Then you’ll taper down over weeks. Stopping suddenly could cause a rebound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2180-08-19 14:39:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll follow up with my GI doctor right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2180-08-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You’re looking better. Pain down to a 3 out of 10?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2180-08-20 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, much better. I’ve had only five bowel movements since yesterday morning, and they’re more formed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2180-08-20 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Your labs this morning show your hemoglobin dropped a bit—to 12.7—but it’s stable. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2180-08-20 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had anemia before. Is it related to Crohn’s?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2180-08-20 10:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, chronic inflammation and poor absorption can cause it. You’re still getting B12 shots monthly, which helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2180-08-20 10:05:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I get those at my GI clinic. Should I keep doing that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2180-08-20 10:06:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, definitely. We’ll send you home with a prescription to continue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we’re discharging you today. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take prednisone 60 mg daily—six 5 mg tablets—and talk to your GI doctor about tapering. Also, omeprazole once daily, loperamide as needed for diarrhea, and your B12 and calcium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, oxycodone-acetaminophen for breakthrough pain, but only as needed. Don’t overuse it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stick to low-residue, lactose-free, caffeine-free foods for now. Gradually reintroduce others as tolerated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:08:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your gastroenterologist within a week to discuss the steroid taper and long-term management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:09:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad we could help. Take care, and call if symptoms return."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—my skin rash. It’s healing, but still itchy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve prescribed bacitracin ointment—apply it twice daily. It should continue improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:13:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll use it as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:14:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. The nurse will bring your discharge papers and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:15:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate everything. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:16:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Get some rest and take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:17:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly to assist with discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2180-08-21 08:21:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2180-08-18 13:23:00",
    "admission_end": "2180-08-21 15:02:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of severe Crohn’s disease, status post subtotal colectomy and ileorectal anastomosis, was admitted for a flare characterized by severe left lower quadrant abdominal pain and frequent watery diarrhea—up to 40 episodes per day. He was initially kept NPO, started on IV fluids and IV steroids, and managed with pain control. Stool studies were negative for infectious causes. He gradually improved, tolerating a clear liquid diet and advancing to low-residue foods, with reduced pain and bowel frequency. He was transitioned to oral prednisone 60 mg daily and discharged home with instructions to follow up with his gastroenterologist for steroid tapering. His GERD was managed with omeprazole, and he was also discharged with loperamide, pain medication, and continued B12 injections.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of small intestine with large intestine",
      "Alkalosis",
      "Acquired absence of intestine (large) (small)",
      "Long-term (current) use of steroids",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
